   "source": "# UHRM prototype (Stage A, Colab): everything in one notebook\n\nRun the cells top to bottom (Runtime > Run all works). Every section is safe to re-run; finished downloads and saved boundaries are reused.\n\n| Section | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | Setup: clone the repo, mount Drive, sign in to Earth Engine |\n| 1 | Access check: Earth Engine, the MODIS collection and its date coverage, Drive |\n| 2 | Study areas: Mumbai and Navi Mumbai boundaries (provisional, from OpenStreetMap) |\n| 3 | Model grid and city masks, with cell counts |\n| 4 | First milestone: fetch one MODIS composite, filter it, map both cities |\n\n**One-time prerequisites:** push the repository to GitHub so section 0 can clone it, and give it your Earth Engine Cloud project id, either by typing it into `EE_PROJECT` in the first code cell or by adding a Colab secret named `EE_PROJECT` (left sidebar, key icon, notebook access on). A project id is not a credential. Never paste passwords or tokens into a cell. If the repo is private, clone with a token kept in a Colab secret instead of the URL below."
  },
