   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import os, subprocess, sys\nREPO_URL = 'https://github.com/Starpredetor/urban-heat-risk-prediction.git'\nREPO_DIR = '/content/uhrm'\nEE_PROJECT = ''   # your Earth Engine Cloud project id (not a secret). Or leave empty and use the Colab secret EE_PROJECT.\n\nif os.path.isdir(REPO_DIR):\n    subprocess.run(['git', '-C', REPO_DIR, 'pull', '--ff-only'], check=True)\nelse:\n    subprocess.run(['git', 'clone', REPO_URL, REPO_DIR], check=True)\nsys.path.insert(0, REPO_DIR + '/src')\nfrom uhrm.colab import bootstrap\nproject = bootstrap(ee_project=EE_PROJECT or None)"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Access check\n",
    "Confirms the collection id in `config/project.yaml` is valid, the band names exist, and shows the real MODIS date coverage (settles SRS open items OI-4 and OI-6)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import ee\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
    "print('Earth Engine OK:', ee.Number(1).add(1).getInfo() == 2)\n",
    "col = ee.ImageCollection(project.modis.collection)\n",
    "print('MOD11A2 composites available:', col.size().getInfo())\n",
    "print('bands:', col.first().bandNames().getInfo())\n",
    "t = col.aggregate_array('system:time_start')\n",
    "first, last = t.reduce(ee.Reducer.min()).getInfo(), t.reduce(ee.Reducer.max()).getInfo()\n",
    "as_date = lambda ms: datetime.fromtimestamp(ms / 1000, timezone.utc).date()\n",
    "print('coverage:', as_date(first), 'to', as_date(last))\n",
    "\n",
    "probe = project.path('_probe.txt')\n",
    "probe.write_text('ok')\n",
    "print('Drive write OK:', probe.read_text() == 'ok', '->', probe)\n",
    "probe.unlink()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Study areas (provisional boundaries)\n",
    "Fetched from OpenStreetMap once and saved to Drive with a provenance file (FR-P1.2). Later runs reuse the saved files. Stage B replaces them with authoritative boundaries verified in QGIS (FR-P1.8).\n",
    "\n",
    "Greater Mumbai is built from the Mumbai City and Mumbai Suburban district polygons. The cell chooses the largest polygon matching each name and checks the area is plausible. If the choice looks wrong, set `MUMBAI_IDS` / `NAVI_MUMBAI_IDS` from the printed candidate list and set `REFRESH_BOUNDARIES = True`. Which Navi Mumbai polygon is right is open item OI-1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from uhrm import boundaries_osm as osm, regions\n",
    "\n",
    "REFRESH_BOUNDARIES = False   # True: search OpenStreetMap again and overwrite the saved files\n",
    "MUMBAI_IDS = None            # optional manual choice, e.g. [1234567, 7654321]\n",
    "NAVI_MUMBAI_IDS = None       # optional manual choice, e.g. [13180880]\n",
    "\n",
    "paths = {a.slug: project.boundary_path(a) for a in project.study_areas}\n",
    "if REFRESH_BOUNDARIES or not all(p.exists() for p in paths.values()):\n",
    "    navi = osm.search('Navi Mumbai')\n",
    "    mumbai = osm.search('Mumbai City district') + osm.search('Mumbai Suburban district')\n",
    "    print('--- Navi Mumbai candidates'); osm.show(navi)\n",
    "    print('--- Mumbai candidates'); osm.show(mumbai)\n",
    "    navi_pick = osm.pick(navi, NAVI_MUMBAI_IDS) if NAVI_MUMBAI_IDS else osm.pick_largest_by_prefix(navi, ['Navi Mumbai'])\n",
    "    mumbai_pick = osm.pick(mumbai, MUMBAI_IDS) if MUMBAI_IDS else osm.pick_largest_by_prefix(mumbai, ['Mumbai City', 'Mumbai Suburban'])\n",
    "    osm.save_boundary(navi_pick, paths['navi_mumbai'], query='Navi Mumbai')\n",
    "    osm.save_boundary(mumbai_pick, paths['mumbai'], query='Mumbai City + Mumbai Suburban districts')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('Using saved boundaries (set REFRESH_BOUNDARIES = True to fetch again).')\n",
    "\n",
    "for slug, p in paths.items():\n",
    "    meta = json.loads(p.with_suffix('.meta.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\n",
    "    print(f\"{slug}: ~{meta['approx_area_km2']:.0f} km2 from\", [s['display_name'][:40] for s in meta['sources']])\n",
    "    # A building or a point has an area near 0; this catches a wrong pick early.\n",
    "    assert 20 < meta['approx_area_km2'] < 3000, f'{slug}: area looks wrong, choose ids by hand (see the candidate list)'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Model grid and city masks\n",
    "A buffered 1 km model domain around both cities (FR-P1.4); the city polygons stay the masks for analysis and metrics. Cell counts show how much data each city really has."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "geoms = {a.slug: regions.load_boundary(project.boundary_path(a), project.grid.crs) for a in project.study_areas}\n",
    "grid = regions.Grid.covering(list(geoms.values()), res=project.grid.model_resolution_m,\n",
    "                             buffer_m=project.grid.domain_buffer_km * 1000, crs=project.grid.crs)\n",
    "masks = {slug: grid.cell_mask(g, project.grid.min_cell_overlap) for slug, g in geoms.items()}\n",
    "for k, v in regions.cell_report(grid, masks).items():\n",
    "    print(f'{k}: {v}')\n",
    "regions.save_grid(grid, project.path('grid.json'))\n",
    "\n",
    "canvas = np.zeros(grid.shape)\n",
    "for i, m in enumerate(masks.values(), start=1):\n",
    "    canvas[m] = i\n",
    "x0, y0, x1, y1 = grid.bounds\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 8))\n",
    "ax.imshow(canvas, extent=(x0, x1, y0, y1), cmap='viridis')\n",
    "for g in geoms.values():\n",
    "    for poly in getattr(g, 'geoms', [g]):\n",
    "        ax.plot(*poly.exterior.xy, 'w-', lw=0.8)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Model domain: 1 km cells assigned to each city')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Check:** both outlines sit where the cities are; `overlap_between_cities` is 0; the grid is large enough for 64 x 64 patches (OI-3). Note the cell counts: small counts limit the statistical power of per-city results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. First milestone: one MODIS LST map per city\n",
    "Fetches a single MOD11A2 composite, saves it as a raw GeoTIFF with a catalogue row (never modified, FR-P2.6), then quality-filters and scales it. Do this before downloading 25 years (FR-P2.9).\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the first real call to Earth Engine's `computePixels`, so an error here is useful feedback about the backend."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from datetime import timedelta\n",
    "from uhrm import acquire, modis\n",
    "from uhrm.backends.earthengine import EarthEngineModis\n",
    "\n",
    "backend = EarthEngineModis(project.modis.collection)\n",
    "start = project.modis.first_milestone_date\n",
    "dates = backend.list_composites(start, start + timedelta(days=40))\n",
    "assert dates, f'no composites found after {start}; check the collection id and date range'\n",
    "day = dates[0]\n",
    "print('composites found:', dates, '| using', day)\n",
    "\n",
    "out_dir = project.path('raw', 'modis')\n",
    "print(acquire.acquire_modis(backend, grid, [day], out_dir, project.path('catalog.csv')))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import rasterio\n",
    "with rasterio.open(acquire.composite_path(out_dir, day)) as src:\n",
    "    dn, qc = src.read(1), src.read(2)\n",
    "lst = modis.process_composite(dn, qc, project.modis.qc)\n",
    "print(f'whole domain: {np.isfinite(lst).mean():.0%} of cells valid')\n",
    "for slug, m in masks.items():\n",
    "    v = lst[m]\n",
    "    ok = np.isfinite(v)\n",
    "    if ok.any():\n",
    "        print(f'{slug}: {m.sum()} cells, {ok.mean():.0%} valid, LST {v[ok].min():.1f} to {v[ok].max():.1f} C, mean {v[ok].mean():.1f} C')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f'{slug}: {m.sum()} cells, none valid on this date')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 7))\n",
    "im = axes[0].imshow(lst, extent=(x0, x1, y0, y1), cmap='inferno')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f'MOD11A2 daytime LST (C), composite starting {day}')\n",
    "fig.colorbar(im, ax=axes[0], shrink=0.7)\n",
    "axes[1].imshow(np.isfinite(lst), extent=(x0, x1, y0, y1), cmap='gray')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('valid cells (white) after quality filter')\n",
    "for ax in axes:\n",
    "    for g in geoms.values():\n",
    "        for poly in getattr(g, 'geoms', [g]):\n",
    "            ax.plot(*poly.exterior.xy, 'c-', lw=0.8)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Milestone checklist\n",
    "- April daytime LST is plausible for land (roughly 30-50 C); the sea is cooler than the land.\n",
    "- The coastline and both outlines line up with the temperature field.\n",
    "- Rejected cells are where cloud or coast would be expected, not a random pattern.\n",
    "- Both cities show some valid cells. If one has none on this date, try another composite before concluding anything.\n",
    "- Download the saved GeoTIFF from Drive and open it in QGIS to confirm it lines up with the boundary. That is the final check for this milestone."
   ]
  }
